# Teaches: a current runs one way, and that is still useful. The locked tee at
# r2c1 has its east mouth against o3 and is refused (level 14's lesson, repeated
# in passing). The long way round arrives at the corridor's FAR end - and from
# there the arrows finally cooperate, carrying water back west to the critter
# sitting in the middle of them. The corridor was never broken. It was backwards.
